node1339 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>safetyRiskAssessment</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/safetyRiskAssessment' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/safetyRiskAssessment</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Results of general safety risk assessment of the AI system.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Results of general safety risk assessment of the AI system.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;Results of general safety risk assessment of the AI system.

Using categorization according to the
EU general risk assessment methodology &lt;https://ec.europa.eu/docsroom/documents/17107&gt;.
The methodology implements Article 20 of Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 and is
intended to assist authorities when they assess general product safety
compliance.

It is important to note that this categorization differs from the one proposed
in the EU AI Act&#x27;s provisional agreement.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
